Making Rodney (and especially Vlad) tougher seems always to be a good
idea. But hard to tell without actually playing it. What I *fear* is
that it might be quite unbalanced (IMO, point 4. is no real balancing
factor); his toughness would hit on the ascension run where lawfuls
are already punished a lot by all the throwbacks in Gehennom, now the
Wizard will also hit very hard on every encounter (and the characters
will require a lot more full healing or stacks of other means to handle
him). And the chaotics will rarely see him and wouldn't suffer as much.

It's already implemented that the Wizard will get tougher from one
resurrection to the next; making him a killer machine each time will
make that existing contrast between the alignments yet much sharper.

